    "created_at": "2016-03-02T20:46:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-02T20:46:14Z",
    "body": "I guess there's no reason that you have to be a cloneable object to have a [[Clone]] method. So I'd instead say:\n\nAll IDL-defined objects have the following internal method: ....\n\nUnless specified otherwise, invoking the [[Clone]] internal method throws a DataCloneError exception. (By default, IDL-defined objects are not cloneable objects.)\n\nWhen specified otherwise, the IDL-defined object is instead a cloneable object. In this case, the [[Clone]] internal method must be defined... It is up to such IDL-defined cloneable objects to define what...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
